LSP ENVELOPE SKEW (acceptance requires this statement)
  The daemon is probed with `mpd/ping` + the renamed envelope (500 ms) and otherwise spawned by this same
  artifact; it lives in ~/.mpd/lsp-daemon/v<version>/. A daemon left over from a pre-rename build does not
  recognise `_mpd`, answers `daemon_authentication_failed` instead of a ping result, so the probe fails, the
  client spawns a fresh daemon, and if the stale process still owns the socket the 5 s readiness wait times
  out with "LSP daemon did not become reachable at <socket>".
  REMEDY: once — `kill $(cat ~/.mpd/lsp-daemon/v<version>/daemon.pid)` (or delete that version directory),
  then retry; the client auto-starts a clean daemon. A dsh restart alone is not enough while the old daemon
  process is alive.

